# Dual-machine iOS shell sprint

Ryan runs **two Cursor chats** (Mac + Windows) with **no shared memory**. Continuity = git on **`test`** + **`WAKEUP`** + **`docs/ios-native-bridge.md`**. Fast agent messages (no git pull to read): **https://lvslotpro.com/theo** … Ryan pings the other chat with `read lvslotpro.com/theo`. Post: `node scripts/theo-channel.mjs post windows "…"`. Spec: **`docs/theo-channel.md`**.

## Ownership

- **Mac:** `ios/` (when present), Xcode, native `EdgeNative` handlers. Do **not** freestyle `src/**` web features.
- **Windows:** `src/**`, web bugs/features, catalog runner / GHA web side. Do **not** edit `ios/**`.
- **Conflict:** Mac wins `ios/`; Windows wins `src/`.

## Bridge

Before adding or renaming `window.EdgeNative.*` on either side, update **`docs/ios-native-bridge.md`**. Stub one side first. Full rules: that doc + **`WAKEUP`** Dual-agent ruleset + **`AGENTS.md`** (`AGENT_RULE_DUAL_MACHINE_IOS`).

## Ritual

Fetch/match **`origin`** before **every** edit (not only session start) → work in lane → commit/push **`test`** → short **`WAKEUP`** note. No `main` / prod without Ryan’s ask. See **`.cursor/rules/sync-origin-before-edit.mdc`**.

